 Penentuan losses teknis merupakan faktor penting yang harus diperhatikan dan dicari penyebabnya, karena berpengaruh terhadap effisiensi jaringan. Metode digunakan pada pembahasan ini adalah perhitungan aliran daya dengan menggunakan alat bantu software EDSA 2005. Hasil perhitungan dipergunakan menentukan besar losses teknis dan perubahan besaran losses teknis apabila dilakukan rekonfigurasi jaringan. Hasil analisis dan perhitungan dengan menggunakan software EDSA 2005, losses teknik penyulang GNDH di jaringan primer tegangan menengah 20 kV pada siang hari beban 2,61 MW losses teknis 2,41 %, pada beban 6,80 MW losses teknis 6,93 %. Penyulang Gunung Dukuh sebelum pelaksanaan rekonfigurasi jaringan pada beban 97,0 MW/hari daya disalurkan di pangkal penyulang 101,51 MW/hari losses teknis 4,51 MW/hari atau 4,44 %, setelah dilakukan rekonfigurasi jaringan pada beban sama daya disalurkan dipangkal penyulang 100,77 MW/hari losses teknis 3,77 MW/hari atau 3,75 %.

Technical losses in medium-voltage primary distribution network is caused by load current in conductor network. Gunung Dukuh (GNDH) is a feeder supplied from Lagadar substation in PT. PLN (Persero) APJ Cimahi. Demand for customer electricity power supplied from distribution transformer influence technical losses of medium-voltage primary network. Gunung Dukuh (GNDH) feeder has radial conductor length from substation to feeder end of 40 km, with supply of power in base is about 220A. Calculation should be done to identify technical losses of GNDH feeder and evaluation of network reconfiguration implementation. Determination of technical losses is important factor that should be considered and its cause is looked for because it influences network efficiency. Method used was power current calculation using software EDSA 2005. Result of calculation was used to determine technical losses and change in technical losses rate when network reconfiguration was done. Result of analysis and calculation using Software EDSA 2005 indicated that at GNDH feeder in 20kV medium-voltage primary network at noon with load of 2,61 MW, technical losses was 2,41%, while at load of 6,80 MW technical losses was 6,93 %. Gunung Dukuh feeder before network reconfiguration at load of 97,0 MW/day, power supplied in feeder base was 101,51 MW/day with technical losses of 4,51 MW/day (4,44 %), after network reconfiguration, at same load, power supplies to feeder base was 100,77 MW/day with technical losses of 3,77 MW/day (3,75 %)', 0, 'OPENALEX', '{"openalex": "https://openalex.org/W1005611088"}', 'NEEDS_REVIEW', 'openalex_20260709T173707Z', '2026-07-17 13:49:46.262812+00', '2026-07-17 13:49:46.262812+00');
power system in the future. Distributed Generation (DG) provides an alternative
to the traditional electricity sources i.e. oil, gas, coal, etc. and can also be used to
enhance electrical power system. Nowaday, the development of DG mostly focus
on renewable energy i.e. small hydro power, solar thermal, photovoltaic, biofuel,
biomass, biogass, wind turbines etc. The DGs are becoming increasingly popular
for their renewable energy, low emission and pollutions, low operations and
maintenance cost, but not in investment cost. One of the main applications of DG
is providing positive impact to the power system. Since the use of DG is getting
developed and giving many advantages, it is very important to study its impact on
distribution network operation.
This research explores the impacts of installing DG on a rural distribution
system. And it focuses on analyzing the impact of DG installation on distribution
network operation including voltage analysis, electric losses and reliability of the
system. At the first section, the voltage impacts of various DG penetration levels
are explored. Secondly, the losses of the system are analyzed. Finally, the
reliability analysis (SAIFI, SAIDI, CAIDI, ENS, and AENS) of the system is
performed by installing DGs.
A rural distribution system in Kulon Progo, DIY Province will be the
object of this research. This Distribution was built using its one-line diagram in
ETAP version 7.0.0 (Electrical Transient Analysis Program) to perform detailed
voltage profile analysis and power losses analysis. The other software is
Microsoft Excel 2007 to perform reliability evaluation. This research uses smallhydro
power potential on Kalibawang irrigation canal for DGs. There are two
locations of small-hydro power potential on the Kalibawang irrigation canal
which has total potential capacities up to 1000 kW. A rural distribution system is
5th feeder of Wates distribution substation which reaches small-hydro power
potential on Kalibawang irrigation canal.
The development of small-hydro power potential in Kalibawang irrigation
canal as DG with capacities up to 1000 kW, will give positive impact to 5th feeder
of Wates substation :
1. Improve voltage profile of the system by 0,596 kV (2,98%).
2. Reduce power losses of the system by 92 kW (26,1%).
3. Improve reliability indices of the system (SAIDI by 14,31%, CAIDI by
14,31% and ENS by 14,04%)', 0, 'OPENALEX', '{"openalex": "https://openalex.org/W1409709681"}', 'NEEDS_REVIEW', 'openalex_20260709T173707Z', '2026-07-17 13:49:46.262812+00', '2026-07-17 13:49:46.262812+00');
distribution network or called on the grid system. Conditional of the
