Electricity tariff is highly influenced by fuel price factor, currency exchange, and inflation. Those factors will affect expense element of the revenue requirement calculations. Revenue requirement is a basic calculation of electricity tariff nominal. Sensitivity analysis could be used to determine how of those factors affects the revenue requirement. Revenue requirement sensitivity toward each factor could be perceived from the sensitivity coefficients. Simulation is started by calculating revenue requirement and mapping each factor correlation on each revenue requirement component. Sensitivity analysis is conducted by varying one of those factors in which the rest is assumed steady. The same case goes for the other factors. Analysis result shows that Rp 100.00 change on US dollar exchange to Rupiah will add the revenue requirement of Rp 7,73 per kWh. The increment of an inflation unit will increase the value of revenue requirement of 13,04 kWh. The simulation of fuel is done by increasing the unit price by 1% for each fuel toward its reference price value. Based on the simulation result, it could be perceived that the value of revenue requirement is the most sensitive toward change of HSD price. For every 1% increment of HSD price will result change in revenue requirement to 20,944%. It is also shown that the margin is not affected by those factors.', 0, 'OPENALEX', '{"openalex": "https://openalex.org/W2625487384"}', 'NEEDS_REVIEW', 'openalex_20260709T173707Z', '2026-07-17 13:49:46.262812+00', '2026-07-17 13:49:46.262812+00');
